LAMMPS (29 Aug 2024 - Update 2)
KOKKOS mode with Kokkos version 4.3.1 is enabled (src/KOKKOS/kokkos.cpp:72)
  using 4 OpenMP thread(s) per MPI task
package kokkos
package kokkos newton on neigh half
### Initialization ###
units si
atom_style molecular
dimension 3
boundary p p p
newton on
#package omp 8
#suffix omp

### System: rigid O2 state pre-generated by gen_o2_init.py ###
read_data o2_init.data
Reading data file ...
  orthogonal box = (0 0 0) to (1e-07 1e-07 1e-07)
  1 by 2 by 2 MPI processor grid
  reading atoms ...
  40000 atoms
  reading velocities ...
  40000 velocities
  scanning bonds ...
  1 = max bonds/atom
  orthogonal box = (0 0 0) to (1e-07 1e-07 1e-07)
  1 by 2 by 2 MPI processor grid
  reading bonds ...
  20000 bonds
Finding 1-2 1-3 1-4 neighbors ...
  special bond factors lj:    0        0        0       
  special bond factors coul:  0        0        0       
     1 = max # of 1-2 neighbors
     0 = max # of 1-3 neighbors
     0 = max # of 1-4 neighbors
     1 = max # of special neighbors
  special bonds CPU = 0.002 seconds
  read_data CPU = 0.260 seconds

### Force field ###
# 2-center LJ O-O atom parameters from Vrabec, Stoll & Hasse, J. Phys. Chem. B 105, 12126 (2001):
#   eps/k_B = 49.60 K -> eps = 6.85e-22 J,  sigma = 3.006e-10 m
pair_style lj/cut 1.0e-9
pair_coeff 1 1 6.85e-22 3.006e-10
special_bonds lj 0.0 0.0 0.0
bond_style zero
bond_coeff 1 1.2075e-10

### Group + per-molecule chunk ###
group o2gas type 1
40000 atoms in group o2gas
compute molchunk o2gas chunk/atom molecule

compute Trot o2gas temp/chunk molchunk com yes adof 1.0 cdof 0.0

# Whole-system kinetic temperature (compute temp accounts for rigid DOF).
compute Ttot all temp

# Decompose:  T_tot = (3 T_trans + 2 T_rot) / 5   =>   T_trans = (5 T_tot - 2 T_rot) / 3
variable Ttrans equal (5*c_Ttot-2*c_Trot)/3

### Neighbor list ###
neighbor     1.0e-10 bin
neigh_modify delay 0 every 20 check yes
atom_modify  sort 100 0.0

### Time integration ###
# rigid O2 (no vibration)
fix myintegrator all rigid/small molecule
  create bodies CPU = 0.004 seconds
  20000 rigid bodies with 40000 atoms
  1.2075002e-10 = max distance from body owner to body atom

### Output ###
thermo 1000
thermo_style custom step v_Ttrans c_Trot c_Ttot ke etotal
thermo_modify lost warn
fix dumpinfo all print 1000 "$(step) $(time) $(v_Ttrans) $(c_Trot)" file output/lammps_O2_energy_relaxation.dat screen no title "timestep simtime Ttrans Trot"

### Run ###
timestep 1.0e-15
run      2000000
Generated 0 of 0 mixed pair_coeff terms from geometric mixing rule
Neighbor list info ...
  update: every = 20 steps, delay = 0 steps, check = yes
  max neighbors/atom: 2000, page size: 100000
  master list distance cutoff = 1.1e-09
  ghost atom cutoff = 1.1e-09
  binsize = 5.5e-10, bins = 182 182 182
  1 neighbor lists, perpetual/occasional/extra = 1 0 0
  (1) pair lj/cut/kk, perpetual
      attributes: half, newton on, kokkos_device
      pair build: half/bin/newton/kk/device
      stencil: half/bin/3d
      bin: kk/device
